  "scope": "Complete unchanged Stall, StallThiefPulse, ThievingOptionPlugin, SkillPulse, Pulse and Quests, compiled with Kotlin 1.8.20/JDK 11 against the pinned ConstLib 1.4.28 artifact. RandomFunction.random(int), StringUtils.isPlusN and the Skills constants are pinned text spliced into adapter shells; RandomFunction.RANDOM returns the case's declared draws. Player (attributes, inCombat, sendMessage, animate, dispatch, the location's region), Skills (getLevel, addExperience), the inventory (freeSlots, add), the packet dispatch, the interaction lock, the saved silk stamp (recorded as its distance from the clock, to the second), Scenery (id, name, isActive, transform), SceneryBuilder.replace, GameWorld.getTicks, RegionManager.getLocalNPCs, NPC (id, sendChat, the combat pulse's isAttacking and attack), Item.getName, playAudio, sendDialogue, isQuestComplete, stun and impact are recording adapters whose results come from declared case state; they are service inputs, not ports. PulseManager.run is an adapter that starts the pulse and records whether it would be submitted: what the manager clears, and what stun's pulseManager.clear() does to the running pulse, are not covered. The driver calls the registered plugin's handle with a scenery of the id a case names and then the pulse's update and stop; no pulse runner, option dispatch, live world, scenery replacement, combat, stun, audio, inventory, experience, quest or dialogue behaviour is established by this corpus.",
